WEBVTT

00:00.162 --> 00:02.379
AI is incredibly useful, but

00:02.325 --> 00:03.199
that doesn't mean we should

00:03.173 --> 00:04.399
throw every piece of private

00:04.259 --> 00:05.609
information we have into it.

00:05.765 --> 00:06.581
I'm going to give you

00:06.508 --> 00:07.448
a few simple rules so

00:07.394 --> 00:08.906
you can use AI aggressively

00:08.766 --> 00:10.793
without being careless with client

00:10.653 --> 00:11.414
information.

00:11.592 --> 00:13.639
Do not paste passwords, Social

00:13.529 --> 00:16.554
Security numbers, bank information, complete

00:16.414 --> 00:19.281
unredacted credit reports, taxpayer data,

00:19.269 --> 00:21.049
or authentication information into an

00:21.018 --> 00:22.443
ordinary AI chat.

00:22.421 --> 00:23.539
If someone could use the

00:23.488 --> 00:25.407
information to access an account,

00:25.267 --> 00:27.007
identify a person, or create

00:26.976 --> 00:28.855
financial harm, it does not

00:28.982 --> 00:30.187
belong in the prompt.

00:30.406 --> 00:32.315
The same common-sense rule applies

00:32.285 --> 00:34.602
to sensitive customer information, private

00:34.532 --> 00:37.426
contracts, and private documents.

00:37.286 --> 00:38.609
Do not assume a real

00:38.469 --> 00:40.090
client record is safe to

00:40.029 --> 00:41.482
paste just because you are

00:41.580 --> 00:42.754
trying to get help with

00:42.614 --> 00:43.082
it.

00:42.942 --> 00:45.120
Keep sensitive operational work in

00:44.980 --> 00:46.571
approved secure systems.

00:46.850 --> 00:48.278
When you are learning, use

00:48.138 --> 00:50.822
redacted or synthetic examples.

00:50.921 --> 00:52.588
Describe the situation without the

00:52.448 --> 00:54.504
private details, replace real names

00:54.364 --> 00:56.270
with fictional ones, and remove

00:56.130 --> 00:57.756
anything the agent is not

00:57.616 --> 00:59.403
authorized to share.

00:59.512 --> 01:00.410
That lets you learn the

01:00.270 --> 01:00.590
workflow

01:01.019 --> 01:02.326
without exposing the people you

01:02.186 --> 01:02.635
serve.

01:02.899 --> 01:04.025
The goal is not to

01:03.885 --> 01:05.357
be afraid of AI.

01:05.318 --> 01:06.292
The goal is to use

01:06.152 --> 01:07.674
it with good judgment.

01:07.778 --> 01:09.524
Give it useful context, keep

01:09.384 --> 01:11.923
confidential information protected, and pause

01:11.783 --> 01:13.306
before you paste anything that

01:13.166 --> 01:14.424
would be a problem if

01:14.284 --> 01:15.725
it appeared somewhere it should

01:15.585 --> 01:15.819
not.
